Stop User-mode Linux VMA walks at the marker a failed fork leaves

When dup_mmap() fails partway, for example because a fatal signal arrives
while a process forks, Linux 6.18 has already copied the parent's whole VMA
tree into the child and stores XA_ZERO_ENTRY over the first VMA it did not
duplicate. Entries from the marker on still point at the parent's VMAs.
exit_mmap() stops at the marker, but the teardown calls tlb_finish_mmu(),
and UML's flush_tlb_mm() walks every entry. It reads vm_end from the marker
itself (address 0x40e) and the guest panics with "Kernel mode fault at addr
0x40e" in flush_tlb_mm called from copy_process. A Harmony node kill that
lands while a process forks reproduces it deterministically.

flush_tlb_mm() and the checkpoint walks over each live address space now
stop at the marker, as exit_mmap() does. Mainline no longer leaves the
marker since commit 43873af772f8 ("mm: change dup_mmap() recovery"), so the
arm64 series, which builds on 7.2-rc4, does not need this patch.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a kernel diff under
consonance/harmony-linux/linux/patches/ per the repository's kernel-patch
exception.

---
--- a/arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c
@@ -167,8 +167,11 @@
 		if (context->id.stack)
 			os_track_mark(__pa(context->id.stack),
 				      STUB_DATA_PAGES * UM_KERN_PAGE_SIZE);
-		for_each_vma(vmi, vma)
+		for_each_vma(vmi, vma) {
+			if (xa_is_zero(vma))
+				break;
 			um_checkpoint_revoke(mm, vma->vm_start, vma->vm_end);
+		}
 	}
 }
 
@@ -194,7 +197,10 @@
 		if (ret < 0)
 			panic("Restoring an address space failed: %d\n", ret);
 		unmap(id, 0, STUB_START);
-		for_each_vma(vmi, vma)
+		for_each_vma(vmi, vma) {
+			if (xa_is_zero(vma))
+				break;
 			um_checkpoint_mark_present(mm, vma->vm_start, vma->vm_end);
+		}
 	}
 }
--- a/arch/um/kernel/tlb.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/tlb.c
@@ -221,6 +221,13 @@
 	struct vm_area_struct *vma;
 	VMA_ITERATOR(vmi, mm, 0);
 
-	for_each_vma(vmi, vma)
+	for_each_vma(vmi, vma) {
+		/*
+		 * A failed dup_mmap() leaves XA_ZERO_ENTRY at the first VMA it
+		 * did not copy. Entries from there on belong to the parent.
+		 */
+		if (xa_is_zero(vma))
+			break;
 		um_tlb_mark_sync(mm, vma->vm_start, vma->vm_end);
+	}
 }
